nals the the Geo and everything  we ported all of the  original geometry from the original  games for those 19 levels and so for the  nostalgic fan and people like yourself  Michael who are you know remembering  that how Tony Hawk's Pro skaters went  into the original games felt I think are  going to be you know pleasantly  surprised and satisfied with how this  game feels because the the geometry is  the same even though we've put you know  all new artwork on it and you know it  have it you know uh presdent 4k all  those things are gonna you know add to  this sort of like meshing of the old and  new in a way that I think people are  gonna be super stoked about I'm  personally excited about it but I do  want to kind of ask about what it's like  to remake a game that had been like  captured such a specific culture back  then and trying to kind of recapture or  kind of capture a new audience in 2020  what what is that like uh yeah I mean we  we really want the game to be authentic  right you know we want it to be true to  the skate culture today I mean great and  you're still a skateboarding superhero  and in this game and you're doing tricks  and combos and you know things that that  are beyond what what most actual skaters  can do but that's the fantasy of being  the skateboarding superhero but beyond  that I mean we really wanted to bring  the the authenticity of the originals  you know the the music and and the  culture to to the fans and I think that  with with skateboarding meant to be in  the Olympics this year which I  unfortunately have been canceled you  know I think that that just speaks  volumes to the the longevity that the  sport has and how it was continuing to  to be a big part of sporting world  I'm Shane can you speak to what it's  like to kind of carry on I guess carry  on that torch of skate culture and going  into thps one and two and joining  these veterans that so many people know  and love yeah well I mean I played the  games you know growing up and loved the  games and it was a big part of what kept  me skateboarding originally because it  was an easy way to learn what the tricks  were to you know obviously as some  wishes saying like do things that are  just you know kind of not possible as  far as me being in the game like I'm  it's hard to explain how exciting that  is to be in that when I was asked to be  a knowledge you know was unbelievable to  be in a new game school to being a  remastered version of the arguably the  best skateboarding game to ever exist is  it's pretty you know huge on us go super  cool can you see I guess Simon can you  speak to the process of relicensing the  music or trying to get that music back  after so long yeah that the process of  licensing the the old tracks from the  previous games I mean as you can expect  in some cases it's difficult 20 years  have gone by and you can't necessarily  track down all of the license ores  sometimes they're potentially you know  disputes over maybe who owns the  copyright but so in general we we wanted  to get everything again we we weren't  able to get a couple of tracks but we  have the vast majority of the songs from  the original Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 1 &amp;  2 games I'm super stoked about that I  mean we've got some of my favorites like  Goldfinger Rage Against the Machine  those songs are so iconic I mean you  still hear so many of the songs from  that soundtrack or from those tracks on  the radio or in television commercials  you know I mean it's just like they're  so everywhere and when you hear them for  for people like me I just instantly  think oh man I  that's Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 1 &amp; 2 I  Cameron you know I used to skate to  those well I used to skate on my  controller to those you know and and  have a blast so yeah I think it's  awesome I think it'll be really cool and  it's  it's a lot different it's a just a  completely different era like back then  I didn't know the names of the songs and  I wasn't gonna go and buy a CD you know  and I'm 11 years old or something so I  think it's really cool that they are the  same songs and we have this access to to  really you know find that yeah it's  funny you mentioned that because on my  11th birthday I actually spent my  birthday money to buy to Bad Religion  CDs because better religion was in Tony  Hawk's Pro Skater - and totally totally  changed my life after that and also I  think Simon I want to ask about using  the likeness of the older versions of  these skaters so I mean Shane you're  gonna be looking young in this game  especially compared to everyone else so  I don't know if you can provide any  insight and select the decision behind  you know keeping their likenesses  current and also having Tony Hawk  wearing wearing pads and the other cover  you know it just seemed to make sense to  have them appear as they currently do  today especially because you know as we  were talking before about sponsorship  and everything a lot of the sponsors  have changed for the original skaters  over the years and so you know putting  them in what they are currently wearing  having them be the personas that they  are today what we felt like was  important and the right way to portray  them with regard to Tony and and pads  and a helmet I mean just in general  having that be one one of the care one  of the appearances of him in the game is  that mean that's how he really looks  when he's skating I mean you know when  when you when you see him on his vert  ramp at his house or at his office it's  like you know he's geared up and so we  wanted that to look authentic as well I  think one of the things I want to ask -  is about move sets and tricks that we'll  be able to do in the game are you  keeping all the tricks from one and two  contained in there or are you also  incorporating some of the new stuff some  of the more modern tricks so yes that we  we have the original tricks  from the from the original Tony Hawk pro  skater one in two games we we also we  added certain things from later in the  series because we wanted to we wanted to  make sure that for people who just think  about the Tony Hawk pro skater series in  general that they they got the  experience that they were expecting and  for example Reaver wasn't introduced  until Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 3 but you  really you really need revert in order  to have the the long combos and to play  the game the way that I think many  people when they think about Tony Hawk  pro skater they're like oh yeah that's  it's like he's an endless combos with  revert and manual and and all these  things and so just simply is more like a  quality of life improvement we wanted to  include things like revert and spine  transfer and acid drop in the game with  regard to other new tricks you know I  mean that we do have new pros in the  game who who we want to make sure that  they have special tricks that represent  their skate style and what they do and  so so you'll get to see that as well  so I would just like to add also I think  it's such a cool take on remastering a  game but also adding a few little things  like that the age thing and and also  just the reboots and then a few other  things that I think will help the game I  actually personally think that's super  cool so these are gonna be faithful  remakes of 1 &amp; 2 but in this day and age  we also have games that are get ongoing  support and get new content added so how  do you plan to support the game after  launch if with anything else I mean we  will support the game launch to make  sure that you know if there are any  issues that need to be be addressed you  know further for the sake of of gameplay  and things like that we have that but  we're right now we're not talking about  any other post launch role can you give  me also before before we dip out of this  I know that multiplayer was actually a  big big part of  the experience and playing things like  like horse or well skate and then just  like trying to rack up the highest score  in two minutes with my friends after  school what can we expect out of  multiplayer modes and online support and  I'm super excited for for this I mean  that we still have two players  split-screen gameplay so for the people  who remember that and love just like  sitting on their sofa and playing with  their friends you totally get that  experience back again and and and we're  super excited for that but we are also  and you know bringing forward into the  game online multiplayer so you'll be  able to play with other people online in  games like trick attack score challenge  combo challenge combo Mombo the various  various games like that from the series  that people remember and and like I  mentioned at the beginning too  you'll be able to share your creative  parks online and you'll be able to skate  in those with your friends as well  that's good to hear so before we take  off I want to kind of throw it to Shane  and Simon is there anything else that  you want to add that we may have not  touched on that you do want to make sure  folks out there know for me I'm just  excited able to get to play it like  myself and it's going to be super cool  infer for me the you know the last thing  that I I want to say is again you know  welcome to Shane and the new pros who  are in the game I'm really excited for  for the the fans not just the old fans  but the new fans to get to to play and  experience those those new skaters and  you know beyond that  September 4th man that's when you can  get it if you if you preorder the game  you can get the the warehouse demo ahead  of time Shane and Simon thank you so  much for taking time out of your day to  talk about Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 1 &amp; 2  remastered it's coming out real soon on  PC epic game store Xbox one and ps4 and  all of you fine folks out there thank  you so much for watch  and we'll see you around because we got  so much more content for GameSpot's play  for all thanks for having us thanks a  lot be safe Michael McShane  [Music]

